S02 browser observation, 13 October 2026 (UTC). Production build (`next start`, port 3000) against real Neon Auth and the Neon database.
No passwords are recorded here. Accounts: Ada Forest (@s01ada, seat 0) and Bea Meadow (@s01bea, seat 1), both created in S01.

Browsers
- Ada: the Cursor IDE browser tab, signed in at localhost:3000.
- Bea: a separate headless Chrome with its own temporary profile, driven over DevTools by tools/s02-second-browser.mjs
  (log: second-browser.log, final screenshot: second-browser-final.png, captured match API responses: second-browser-network.jsonl).
  Neon Auth refused sign-in from the origin 127.0.0.1, so both browsers used localhost.
- Moves were made by clicking the real UI controls from small in-page scripts (resolve the pending choice, try one species per turn,
  otherwise end deployment and end the turn). The play strategy was scripted; every command went through the browser UI and API.

1. Matchmaking and admission
- Ada entered the casual queue from /play; Bea entered from her browser. Both pages were redirected into the same match
  30232111-6158-45c0-ba44-55c1bd353ced (second-browser.log 11:51:58, match-id.txt).

2. Concurrent duplicate and stale commands (from Ada's tab, against Neon)
- Five simultaneous POSTs with the same commandId and body: exactly one reply had duplicate:false; the other four returned the same
  receipt with duplicate:true. The match version moved 3 -> 4 once.
- Three POSTs with a stale expectedVersion each returned 409 with the current version 4.

3. Reconnect
- Ada's tab was reloaded mid-match: version, her hand and the deadline (11:53:35.640Z) were identical before and after.
  Mid-match board screenshot: ada-board-midmatch.png.

4. Complete persisted match
- Play continued in both browsers until the engine finished the game at version 59 (59 accepted commands, none automatic).
- Bea's page: "You won on final score (18-0) · casual rating 1000 -> 1016" (second-browser.log 11:57:03).
- Ada's page after reload: "Bea Meadow won on final score (0-18) · casual rating 1000 -> 984" (ada-match-finished.png).
- /history for Ada: "Loss vs s01bea · Casual · final score 0-18 · Rating 1000 -> 984 · 2026-10-13 11:57 UTC · Replay".
- /leaderboard: 1. Bea Meadow (@s01bea) 1016, 1 game; 2. Hidden player 984, 1 game (Ada's profile is not public) (leaderboard.png).
  Each rating changed once and the games count is 1 for each player.
- Replay from Ada's seat: opens at "Step 0 of 59"; End shows "Step 59 of 59 · You: pass · Bea Meadow won on final score (0-18)",
  with the same board as the live finished view (ada-replay-final-step.png).

5. Hidden information in both network views
- Bea: 40 match API responses captured from her browser (9 full views, 8 command replies, 22 unchanged polls, 1 stale-version 409).
- Ada: her live finished view and the replay at step 30 (mid-match, Bea holding 6 cards), fetched from her tab
  (ada-browser-network.jsonl). The public `moves` list (step, seat and command type) was trimmed from the replay body, and the
  step-59 replay was not kept because its game is identical to the live view.
- tools/s02-leak-check.mjs rebuilt every authoritative state from the stored seed and commands (rebuilt version 59 = stored 59) and
  checked each response against the true state at its version: no opponent hand cards, no deck cards, no seed, rng, deck,
  eventDeck, private_snapshot or accepted keys, and the player's own hand equal to the truth. Result: pass (leak-check.log).

Defects found during observation and fixed
- The Cursor tab stopped polling after it was briefly treated as hidden: the poller returned without rescheduling and waited for a
  visibilitychange event that the embedded view never sent. Hidden tabs now keep a slow check without making requests.
- Neon Auth was intermittently unreachable (5 of 6 rapid requests from Ada's tab got 401 while she was signed in). The session lookup
  now retries, and an unreachable provider returns 503 instead of 401, so the match page shows "Connection lost; reconnecting…"
  and command retries keep the same commandId. After the rebuild Ada's match, replay, history and leaderboard pages loaded normally.

Not observed: a private-room match between the two browsers (covered by tests/session-S02.test.mjs), and a timeout forfeit in a
browser (covered by the R26 test). No deployment.
